course: dictionary
lesson: 2688
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives each meaning a number, and the words around the word tell you which one is meant. Diesel is a good example: it can be a fuel, a vehicle, or a name.
explain: «Electric trains take their power from overhead wires; diesel trains carry their own engine.» Here diesel is a kind of train, so it means a vehicle or engine that uses diesel fuel. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence best.
explain: Capital letters help too. «Jake's dog Diesel is huge and scruffy» has a capital D, so Diesel is a name here, not a fuel. Check the clues, then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: Diesel is a heavy fuel made from oil, used in many trucks, buses, trains, tractors and some cars.
fact: A diesel is a vehicle or engine that uses diesel fuel.
fact: Diesel is named after Rudolf Diesel, the engineer who invented the diesel engine.
fact: At a petrol station you choose petrol or diesel, and putting the wrong one in a car can break it.
fact: Diesel is a fossil fuel that gives out carbon dioxide and pollution, so many towns want electric buses instead.
exercise: «The lorry needed more diesel before the long trip.» What is diesel here? | A wire above the track | *A heavy fuel made from oil | A kind of tiny explosion | A dog's name
exercise: «Jake's dog Diesel is huge and scruffy.» What is Diesel here? | A vehicle that uses diesel fuel | A heavy fuel made from oil | *A dog's name, with a capital D
exercise: «The old diesel rumbled slowly past the station.» What does diesel mean here? | A fuel that gives out light | *A train or other vehicle that runs on diesel fuel | A dog who sleeps on your feet
test: «Many towns want electric buses because diesel gives out pollution.» In this sentence, what is diesel? | A kind of cloud | A name | *A fuel made from oil | A dog
test: Which fact is about Rudolf Diesel? | *He was the engineer who invented the diesel engine | He was a famous footballer | A dog named after him
exam: In «Jake takes Diesel for a long walk instead of shouting at anyone», what is Diesel? | *A name, the dog's name | A vehicle | A fuel made from oil | A kind of engine
